# Scenario: positioned effects at mirrored positions (SCENARIO=sound_pan tests/boot_smoke.py; docs/OPENAL_MIGRATION_PLAN.md
# section 4.6): the hero standing still in front of the castle, the music and looping effects faded out, while
# DOTHEROES_DEV_SOUND (port/audio_hooks.cpp, `sepos`) asks the game's own sound manager for an effect at the
# listener's position plus an offset (the game's frame: +x right, +y up, +z forward), the same offset mirrored next,
# in ABBA order -- the same calls on either audio path, its output captured (AUDIO_WAV for FMOD's, OpenAL Soft's
# wave writer for the native one) and measured per channel (tools/pan_check.py).
#
# The steps (seconds after the sound manager's first update), 1.2 s apart from 96 s:
#   effect 202 (221_knock: the sword striking; the game places it on the hero's facing axis at the contact, 0.3
#   up): 8 pairs at x -1.5/+1.5; 4 pairs at -4/+4; 4 pairs at -12/+12 (beyond the list's min distance, 8.8);
#   4 pairs ahead/behind (z +1.5/-1.5); 4 pairs at 45 degrees ahead (x -1.06/+1.06, z 1.06)
#   effect 302 (375_hit_01: a blow landing, placed at the enemy): 4 pairs at x -1.29/+1.29 (y 0.17, z -0.27, as
#   traced)
#   effect 148 (156_Anchor_throw: the swing, played by the game without a position), 4 times; effect 202 without
#   a position, 4 times (the centred references)
#
# Starts from: the kept checkpoint castle-front (CONTINUE: field area 17).
#! saves build/checkpoints/castle-front
#! env DOTHEROES_NATIVE_CD=1 DOTHEROES_NATIVE_SOLVER=1,2,4,5,6 GCM_WRAP_LAP=1 DOTHEROES_PRESENT_ONCE=1
#! env DOTHEROES_DEV_STATE=1 DIAG_FRAMES=frames.log PS3_VERBOSE=0
#! env WINDOW=1 VISIBLE=1 TOPMOST=1 GRAB_EVERY=60 PS3_OSD_FPS=2 DUMP=0 SHOT_EVERY=0
